-- title:
--   Translation preserves inclusion of sets
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a normed additive commutative group, let $S \subseteq T \subseteq E$, and let $x \in E$. Writing $S[x] = \{\,y : y - x \in S\,\} = x + S$ for the translate of $S$ by $x$, one has
--   $$S[x] \;\subseteq\; T[x].$$
--
--   This is the monotonicity of the translation operator, the elementary fact used whenever an inclusion between cones (say a cone of smaller aperture inside one of larger aperture) has to be transported to the cones based at a given point.
